course: dictionary
lesson: 14158
title: Mistakenly and honest errors
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mistakenly is an adverb. It tells you how something was done or how someone thinks. Its clue is the word mistake, and -ly tells you it describes an action. So mistakenly means in a wrong way, by accident.
explain: «I mistakenly sent the message to the wrong person.» The sender did not mean to send it to that person. The word mistakenly tells us it was an honest error, not a choice. Swap in "by mistake" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Mistakenly can also describe a belief. «Many people mistakenly think bulls hate red.» Here it means believing something that is not true. Look for clue words like think and believe, which often come just before mistakenly.
fact: Mistakenly is an adverb, so it tells how an action happens or how someone thinks.
fact: «Mistakenly» means because of a mistake, or wrongly.
fact: «Mistakenly» can also mean believing something that is not true.
fact: Phrases to spot: «mistakenly believe», «mistakenly think», «mistakenly took».
fact: A good check: swap in "by mistake" or "wrongly" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «He mistakenly took my bag.» What does mistakenly tell us? | He hid the bag under the bed | He took the bag on purpose | He gave the bag back to me | *He took the bag by mistake
exercise: «Many people mistakenly think bulls hate red.» What does mistakenly show? | *The belief is not true | The people are very clever | The belief is proven by science | The bulls are angry
exercise: «The shopkeeper mistakenly gave me the wrong change.» What does mistakenly mean? | Angrily, after a long argument | *Wrongly, by accident | Kindly, to help me | Slowly, with great care
test: «Some people mistakenly believe that goldfish have a three-second memory.» What does mistakenly mean here? | On purpose, to make a joke | Quickly, in a hurry | *Believing something that is not true | Happily, with a smile
test: «She mistakenly put salt in her tea.» Which phrase could replace mistakenly without changing the meaning? | Happily | *By mistake | On purpose | Very slowly
exam: Which phrase best matches the meaning of mistakenly? | *By mistake | Very loudly | Long ago | On purpose
